        "input": "",
        "output": "",
        "explanation": "Your task is to answer QQQ queries. For the ithi^{th}ith query:\nYou are given an integer SiS_iSi​ and you need to find a mountain with sum SiS_iSi​.\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains three space-separated integers NNN, MMM, and QQQ, the dimensions of the matrix and the number of queries.\nThe second line contains QQQ space-separated integers S1,S2,…,SQS_1,S_2,\\ldots,S_QS1​,S2​,…,SQ​, denoting each query.\nOutput Format\n\nFor each query, if no possible mountain with given sum exists, output −1-1−1.\nOtherwise, output two lines:\n\nThe first line contains two space-separated integers PPP,KKK (1≤P≤N,P+K−1≤N)(1 \\leq P \\leq N,P+K-1 \\leq N)(1≤P≤N,P+K−1≤N);\nThe second line contains KKK space-separated integers L1,L2,…,LK(1≤Li≤M)L_1,L_2,\\ldots,L_K(1 \\leq L_i \\leq M)L1​,L2​,…,LK​(1≤Li​≤M).\n\n\n\nIf multiple mountains satisfy the condition, you may print any."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5 4 4\n20 36 1 60",
        "output": "2 3\n2 4 1\n1 5\n3 1 4 1 3\n1 1\n1\n1 5\n4 4 4 4 4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nQuery 111: A possible mountain that satisfies the condition is highlighted below:\n\nHere, P=2P = 2P=2 and K=3K = 3K=3 and we are selecting 2,4,2, 4,2,4, and 111 cells from the second, third, and fourth row respectively. The sum of the highlighted cells is 202020.\nQuery 222: A possible mountain that satisfies the condition is highlighted below:\n\nHere, P=1P = 1P=1 and K=5K = 5K=5 and we are selecting 3,1,4,1,3, 1, 4, 1,3,1,4,1, and 333 cells from the first, second, third, fourth and fifth rows respectively. The sum of the highlighted cells is 363636."
      }
